{
  "info": {
    "name": "Promotion Management API",
    "description": "Catalog + promotion API with read-time effective pricing, keyset pagination, versioned Redis caching and a chunked CSV ingest pipeline.\n\n**Before running:** `docker compose up -d && npm run migrate && npm run seed && npm run dev`. The seed creates categories and products; there is no category endpoint, so the collection picks `categoryId` up from the first listing response.\n\n**Run order matters.** Requests chain through collection variables (`categoryId`, `productId`, `productBId`, `promotionId`, `cursor`, `jobId`). Use the Collection Runner top to bottom, or send them by hand in folder order.\n\nMoney is always a decimal string (`\"19.99\"`). JSON numbers for money are rejected with 400. Every error is `{ error: { code, message, details? }, requestId }`.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "productBId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "sku",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "cursor",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "promotionId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "categoryPromotionId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "startsAt",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "endsAt",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "jobId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "test",
      "script": {
        "exec": [
          "pm.test(\"x-request-id header present\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.headers.has(\"x-request-id\")).to.be.true);"
        ],
        "type": "text/javascript"
      }
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Operational",
